## Design adapted from other projects

Two projects informed designs in this repository. No source file was copied: the implementations here are
TypeScript, and each adapted file carries a header naming its source and the commit. Their licences are recorded
here, as they require.

### MCP Clearsight

- Repository: https://github.com/cesar-alves/mcp-clearsight, read at commit 4912ede.
- Licence: MIT OR Apache-2.0, © 2026 The MCP Clearsight contributors.
- Adapted as design, with the weight and threshold values carried over as data:
  - `src/registry.ts`, `docs/tool-parity.md` — one tool registry projected to every surface (`features.md` §4.1, §4.7).
  - `src/capabilities.ts` — a capability contract that never advertises what the build cannot do (§4.7).
  - `src/recommend/traits.ts`, `src/recommend/rank.ts` — the ranking design: hard filters, `intent` 0.35 /
    `data_fit` 0.40 / `expressiveness` 0.25, a total order, confidence bands, near ties and abstention (§4.9).
  - `test/recommend.test.ts`, `eval/recommend.cases.ts` — cases graded by musts and must-nots (`evals/README.md`).
  - `docs/status.md` — status that names what does not work as carefully as what does.

### Rune

- Repository: https://github.com/anomalyco/rune, read at commit bca47138.
- Licence: MIT, © Anomaly.
- Adapted as design:
  - `src/figure.ts` — the figure as a semantic tree with stable ids, plus set-of-marks numbers on the picture
    (`research/16-research-agent-generative-ui.md` §3–§4).
  - `src/themes/palette.ts` — series colours spread so neighbours differ, derived in OKLCH from the theme's own
    lightness and chroma, and label ink taken from the fill's lightness (`crates/rune-mermaid/src/chart.rs`).
  - `docs/architecture.md` — the exact and the within-tolerance determinism promise
    (`research/14-research-determinism-verification.md` §1–§2).
